{"name":"Yule Tree","hex":"#66b032","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yule","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Yule."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yule"},{"term":"tree","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial woody plant taller and larger than a shrub with a wooden trunk and, at some distance from the ground, having leaves and branches.","Any other plant (such as a large shrub or herb) that is reminiscent of the above in form and size."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To chase (an animal or person) up a tree.","To place in a tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Christmas tree","blocks":[{"text":"A Christmas tree is a decorated tree, usually an evergreen conifer such as a spruce, pine or fir, associated with the celebration of Christmas. It may also be an artificial tree of similar appearance."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/A1_Christmas_Tree_photo.jpg/330px-A1_Christmas_Tree_photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christmas_tree","wikidata":"Q47128"},{"title":"Yule","blocks":[{"text":"Yule is a winter festival and time of the year historically observed by pagan Germanic peoples that was later merged with the festival of Christmas during the process of Christianisation. The oldest accounts describe two Yule-months around the winter solstice in early Germanic calendars."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Drinking_scene_on_an_image_stone.jpg/330px-Drinking_scene_on_an_image_stone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yule","wikidata":"Q211945"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usag